 "notes": "Ras Disha, the northern cape of Makadi Bay: the fringing reef round the cape, the sand south of it at 10-12 m with the three ergs (the northernmost with the small glassfish tunnel at about 5 m), the coral ledge at 12-15 m and the drop-off on the east. Shoreline from OpenStreetMap; the erg positions are inferred from dive-centre descriptions (redseacreatures.com, funnydivers.com), so they, the reef edge, the mooring and the loop are approximate. Coastline © OpenStreetMap contributors (ODbL).",
